+
+## 2026-11-02: headings of included pages no longer get section edit links (#44623)
+
+Headings that come from the output of a macro (for example `{{include(Page)}}`) got "Edit this section" links and were counted as sections of the page, so the section numbers of the local headings after the include did not match the numbers used when editing. Macros now take the option `:sections => true` when they are defined (only `collapse` uses it). The output of other macros is wrapped in markers while the page is rendered, `parse_sections` skips the headings between the markers, and the markers are removed at the end of the outermost `textilizable` call. Nested macros (an include inside a collapse) work because the markers are only removed when no macro is running.
+
+Learned: `exec_macro` output is escaped unless it is `html_safe`, so test macros must return `html_safe` strings. Textile and Markdown differ: a test page that includes a textile page must itself use textile.
+
+Left: the included headings still get anchors and appear in the table of contents, as before. This change does not decide whether they should.
